    fix: map booking error codes to correct HTTP statuses and document ghost-booking cleanup
    
    - HOLD_EXPIRED  -> 422 Unprocessable Entity (hold timed out, user must re-select seat)
    - NOT_YOUR_HOLD -> 403 Forbidden (hold belongs to a different user)
    - ALREADY_BOOKED -> 409 Conflict (seat already confirmed in DB)
    - Unknown failures -> 500 Internal Server Error
    Previously all failures collapsed to 409, making HOLD_EXPIRED and NOT_YOUR_HOLD
    indistinguishable from seat conflicts on the frontend.
    
    Also adds a commented-out ghost-booking cleanup query to schema.sql for one-time
    manual execution: cancels CONFIRMED bookings silently inserted during the 500 era
    (when the missing-column bug caused findBookingById to throw after a successful INSERT).

