Author: Prynshumishra <prynshu09@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun May 17 12:55:26 2026 +0530

    fix: resolve all production-level bugs
    
    1. schema.sql – Add ALTER TABLE migrations for columns missing in older
       production DBs (booked_at, cancelled_at, refund_status, refund_amount
       on bookings; auth_provider, google_id, avatar_url, is_email_verified,
       is_active, last_login_at on users). Fixes the 500 on POST /book.
       Also resets is_active=1 for users deactivated by a bad migration default,
       fixing the 401 on login for all existing accounts.
    
    2. schema.sql + application.properties – Enable spring.sql.init.continue-on-error
       so ALTER TABLE statements fail silently on databases that already have the
       column (MySQL <8.0 compatibility).
    
    3. EmailService.java + AsyncConfig.java – Mark all three email methods
       @Async("emailTaskExecutor") and add a dedicated ThreadPoolTaskExecutor.
       Forgot-password now returns immediately instead of blocking on SMTP.
    
    4. AuthController.java – Replace hard-coded secure(false)/SameSite=Lax with
       SECURE_COOKIE env var (defaults true). In production the cookies are now
       Secure + SameSite=None, which is required for cross-origin cookie delivery
       between the Vercel frontend and the Render backend.
    
    5. TravelsService.java – Replace redis.get() + redis.delete() with the atomic
       redis.getAndDelete() so two concurrent booking requests from the same user
       cannot both claim the same hold, eliminating the double-booking race condition.
    
    6. TravelsRepository.java – Rewrite confirmBooking INSERT as
       INSERT … SELECT … WHERE NOT EXISTS (CONFIRMED booking for same seat+date)
       providing a DB-level safety net. Returns -1 when the seat was already taken
       so the service layer can return ALREADY_BOOKED instead of a 500.

